   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing region by region; I could not run it through a parser here, so the ring closures and stereo marks were checked by hand only.\n\n**Fragments, left to right**\n- **Benzothiophene:** a benzothiophene-2-carboxamide carrying a CF2\u2013PO3H2 group at C5.\n- **Bicyclic core:** an 8-membered ring (N, CH2, CH(NH-acyl), C=O, N, CH, CH2, CH2) fused to a pyrrolidine. The ring nitrogen carries a CH2CH2NMe2 chain, and the pyrrolidine C2 carries a carboxamide.\n- **Arginine residue:** NH\u2013CH(CH2CH2CH2\u2013NH\u2013C(=NH)NH2)\u2013C=O.\n- **Phenylalanine residue:** NH\u2013CH(CH2\u2013C6H4\u2013tBu, para)\u2013C=O, whose carbonyl is bonded to a piperazine nitrogen.\n- **Linker and E3 ligand:** the other piperazine nitrogen carries \u2013CH2CH2CH2\u2013NH\u2013, which is attached to C4 of a 2-(2,6-dioxopiperidin-3-yl)isoindolin-1-one.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\n- I assigned the five wedged centres from the wedge geometry: the amide-bearing ring carbon, the ring-fusion CH, the pyrrolidine C2, the Arg \u03b1-carbon and the Phe \u03b1-carbon.\n- The piperidinedione C3 is drawn with plain bonds, so it has no stereo mark.\n\nSMILES: OP(O)(=O)C(F)(F)c1ccc2sc(cc2c1)C(=O)N[C@H]1CN(CCN(C)C)CC[C@H]2CC[C@@H](C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCNC(=N)N)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc3ccc(cc3)C(C)(C)C)C(=O)N3CCN(CCCNc4cccc5C(=O)N(C6CCC(=O)NC6=O)Cc45)CC3)N2C1=O"
